{# The contents of a book, as Chromium can print it.

   Chromium does not know where anything lands until the layout is finished, so
   this list is links only — the same shape the built-in engine produces. Deep
   items exist only when `toc_depth` allows them, which is also when they stop
   being demoted to paragraphs.

   The title is an <h1> so that the outline has an entry for the contents, and
   so that it sorts above the articles rather than nowhere at all. #}
<div class="pdf-toc">
    <h1 class="pdf-toc-title">{{ 'PLUGIN_PDF.TOC'|t }}</h1>

    <ul class="pdf-toc-list">
        {% for item in toc %}
            <li class="pdf-toc-level-{{ item.level }}">
                <a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.text }}</a>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</div>
